Prescott and his world-class upper crust school tick, and [The Rector of Justin](https://bookshop.org/a/14860/9780618224890) takes off.\n\nAspinwall seems surprised to learn that 
Prescott is an intellectual and a progressive given the focus on sports, strict discipline, and religious tradition at the school. But many more surprises await. As the novel unspools
we learn from other sources who come into Aspinwall’s orbit. Eventually Aspinwall is given files and documents by others and he takes on the task of possibly writing Prescott’s 
biography.\n\nThe book is breezy and warmly inviting, despite its substantial and ethically weighty themes. I found it an absolute pleasure. The characters are all interesting, and in
